    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0564" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg468"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Buck to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo,
                                Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1899-06-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 17, 1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 310.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    translation of an Imperial ordinance, dated the 14th instant, bringing into
                    operation the new treaties between Japan and other powers.</p>
                <p>It will be observed that the French and Austro-Hungarian do not come into
                    operation until August 4 next, while all the others take effect on July 17.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. E. Buck.</hi></signed></closer>




